[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827788386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105636#issuecomment-2827788386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105636","id":2827788386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ojKBi","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-24T14:14:42Z","updated_at":"2025-04-24T14:14:42Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2827788386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2955819788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105636#issuecomment-2955819788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105636","id":2955819788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wLjsM","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T13:36:44Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T13:37:31Z","body":"In retrospect, I think this may not have been the right way to go.\r\n\r\nA few weeks ago, I did a game jam using only the Android editor (on a Meta Quest 3), and I was able to use the \"Remote deploy\" button to run and test the WebXR version of our game.\r\n\r\nThere was one issue: the \"Run in Browser\" button didn't actually open the browser, but it did start the web server, and the other options (\"Start HTTP server\", \"Re-export project\", and \"Stop HTTP server\") did work fine. I only had to type the URL into the web browser myself (which I knew, but a normal user probably wouldn't ;-)).\r\n\r\nSo, overall, I'm now of the opinion that we should show this button on the Android editor. If there's particular platforms that won't work there, we should disable those platforms individually.\r\n\r\nAnd I'll see if I can figure out how to fix opening the browser on Android too, so that we have a platform (Web) that we know is fully working :-)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2955819788/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2957441490","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105636#issuecomment-2957441490","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105636","id":2957441490,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wRvnS","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-10T01:33:07Z","updated_at":"2025-06-10T01:33:07Z","body":"My main objective was to reduce the width profile of the Android editor and remote debug button seemed unusable, so I targeted it for removal. I'm fine with bringing it back if we can resolve the web issue.\r\n\r\n> And I'll see if I can figure out how to fix opening the browser on Android too, so that we have a platform (Web) that we know is fully working :-)\r\n\r\nOS.shell_open(...) `OS.shell_open(\"https://godotengine.org\")` should be enough for opening any link, not sure if it's already used though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2957441490/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2960570492","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105636#issuecomment-2960570492","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105636","id":2960570492,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wdrh8","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-10T21:00:51Z","updated_at":"2025-06-10T21:06:24Z","body":"> OS.shell_open(...) `OS.shell_open(\"https://godotengine.org\")` should be enough for opening any link, not sure if it's already used though.\r\n\r\nIt turns out that this is what it's already doing.\r\n\r\nI just did some testing on my Android tablet (with Godot 4.4.1), and actually, the \"Run in Browser\" button works perfectly fine there! I was able to run the 2D Platformer Demo exported to the web from the editor.\r\n\r\nI also tried to the same on Pico 4 Ultra (also with Godot 4.4.1), and it worked there too!\r\n\r\nSo, it seems that it's only on Meta Quest that  `OS.shell_open(\"https://...\")` isn't working - probably a bug in HorizonOS.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I think we should revert this PR, and things should eventually start working on Meta Quest after they fix the bug. I just posted PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107378 to do the revert","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2960570492/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]